+// [barreplay] P4: <tempNum> < 0 takes the next synced tempNum here as before;
+// otherwise it is the number the main thread took for this search in order.
+// <mtThread> >= 0 runs the search on that pool thread (BrPipeTarget.h): the
+// quad query uses its pools and the dedup marks are its per-thread marks
+// (mtTempNum), so the units' synced tempNum is left alone. Nothing compares
+// a unit's tempNum with any number but the one its own scan just took, so
+// the marks a search does not leave behind are never missed.
